<script>
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Registry from '#src/lib/Registry.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc>
    <Section title="A link names a route, and `url` fills it in">
        <p>The CRM's companies list links each company with
            <code>url('/companies/[id=SLUG]', &#123; id: company.id &#125;)</code>. You write the pattern a
            page is filed under, matcher and all, rather than the address, and <code>url</code> fills in
            the segments.
            Leaving out a required one is a compile error, and a pattern no page is filed under is
            refused by <code>abide check</code>. A query follows the params:
            <code>url('/companies', &#123;&#125;, &#123; city: 'London' &#125;)</code>. Pass its
            defaults after it, and a member at its default is left out of the address.</p>

        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>What it does for the CRM</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>Routes</code></td><td>every pattern the CRM files a page under, and every public file's address, declared by <code>abide check</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>RouteLiteral</code></td><td>one of those patterns: what <code>url</code> takes</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Query</code></td><td>the query argument, a record or a <code>URLSearchParams</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>ParamsOf&lt;P&gt;</code></td><td>the params object pattern <code>P</code> takes</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>HasParams&lt;P&gt;</code></td><td>whether <code>P</code> requires one</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>HasSegments&lt;P&gt;</code></td><td>whether <code>P</code> has any bracketed segment</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>RequiredNames&lt;P&gt;</code></td><td>its <code>[name]</code> segments</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>OptionalNames&lt;P&gt;</code></td><td>its <code>[[name]]</code> segments</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>RestNames&lt;P&gt;</code></td><td>its <code>[...name]</code> segments</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <p>You never write the last six. They are how <code>url</code>'s signature is read off the
            pattern, and a compile error naming <code>RequiredNames</code> is naming the segment you
            left out.</p>
    </Section>

    <Registry />
</Doc>
